@Test public void testIteratorHasNext() {
    Attributes a = new Attributes();
    a.put("Tot", "1");
    a.put("Hello", "2");
    a.put("data-name", "3");

    int seen = 0;
    for (Attribute attribute : a) {
        seen++;
        assertEquals(String.valueOf(seen), attribute.getValue());
    }
    assertEquals(3, seen);
}

proposals.refactored:
private static final String VALUE_ONE = "1";
private static final String VALUE_TWO = "2";
private static final String VALUE_THREE = "3";
private static final int EXPECTED_COUNT = 3;

@Test
public void testIteratorHasNext() {
    Attributes a = new Attributes();
    a.put("Tot", VALUE_ONE);
    a.put("Hello", VALUE_TWO);
    a.put("data-name", VALUE_THREE);
    verifyAttributesIteration(a);
}

private void verifyAttributesIteration(Attributes attrs) {
    int seen = 0;
    for (Attribute attribute : attrs) {
        seen++;
        assertEquals(
            "Attribute value at position " + seen + " should be " + seen,
            String.valueOf(seen),
            attribute.getValue()
        );
    }
    assertEquals(
        "Total number of attributes should be " + EXPECTED_COUNT,
        EXPECTED_COUNT,
        seen
    );
}

smells.ConditionalTestLogic:
Extract the for‑each loop (the only control‑flow construct) into a private helper method. Example:
```java
private void verifyAttributesIteration(Attributes attrs) {
    int seen = 0;
    for (Attribute attr : attrs) {
        seen++;
        assertEquals(String.valueOf(seen), attr.getValue(), "Attribute value at position " + seen + " should be " + seen);
    }
    assertEquals(EXPECTED_COUNT, seen, "Total number of attributes should be " + EXPECTED_COUNT);
}
```
Then the test simply calls `verifyAttributesIteration(a);`.

smells.MagicNumberTest:
Introduce well‑named constants for all literal numbers used in the test. Example:
```java
private static final String VALUE_ONE = "1";
private static final String VALUE_TWO = "2";
private static final String VALUE_THREE = "3";
private static final int EXPECTED_COUNT = 3;
```
Use these constants in the setup and assertions:
```java
a.put("Tot", VALUE_ONE);
...
assertEquals(EXPECTED_COUNT, seen, ...);
```

